{"t":1793767145182,"lane":"1","type":"agent.say","text":"The tickets are booked and paid. Booking reference **HL-EFQTJZ**. I only paid after you said yes on the yes card.\n\n- **When:** Saturday 7 November. You leave the Gateway of India at 09:30 and reach Elephanta at 10:30. The return leaves Elephanta at 14:00 and gets back at 15:00.\n- **Seats:** Upper deck, 3.20 USDC a person, which is under your 4 USDC limit. Asha Rao has U22, Leo Marin U23, Mei Tan U24 and Sam Okoye U25.\n- **Boarding:** Gateway jetty 4, the step-free one. Boarding help for Sam is on the booking: \"Sam Okoye uses a cane: please help with boarding\". It costs nothing.\n- **Total:** 12.80 USDC, about 1,126 INR. This is on the Arbitrum Sepolia test network, so no real money moved.\n- **Transaction:** https://sepolia.arbiscan.io/tx/0xfa7b9083ab5f50dbb87ac51cbc2bf4890f8ee6ced2dc6d2005d1c279c41bd1b7\n- **Cancellation:** free until Friday 6 November at 18:00, with the refund going back to the same wallet. To cancel, run `./bin/ferry refund o-ws5bt3`.\n\nChoices I made:\n- **Outbound 09:30:** On Saturday the 09:00 upper deck is sold out, and the 10:00 has only 2 upper-deck seats left. The 09:30 was the only time in your window with upper-deck seats for all four.\n- **Return 14:00:** I read \"back after 14:00\" as the 14:00 return or later. If you meant strictly later than 14:00, the next return is 15:30, but the booking would need changing.\n- **First quote dropped:** My first quote's help note called Sam \"him\", and you hadn't told me Sam's pronouns. I threw that quote away and booked with neutral wording."}
